<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rudolf I of Germany</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1218–1291</span> · Also known as Rudolf of Habsburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rudolf I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, a Swabian count of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> family, was elected King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> in 1273, ending the Great Interregnum after the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a>. He defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottokar-ii-of-bohemia">Ottokar II of Bohemia</a> in 1278 and gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a> to his sons, founding Habsburg power there. He recovered royal lands and confirmed the rights of many towns as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/free-imperial-city">free imperial cities</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rudolf-i-of-germany.jpg" alt="Rudolf I of Germany" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wolfgang Sauber · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kaiser_Rudolf_I._1275.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
